  "hue": {
    "note": "One hue, many scopes. Any element can set --cipher-hue (a number of degrees) and data-hue (subtle or pop), and every descendant reads hue-icon, hue-tint, hue-soft and hue-fill built from that hue on the ramp below. Lightness and chroma are fixed per scheme and level, so no hue comes out louder than another. These tokens hold the oklch lightness and chroma pairs; the colors themselves only exist inside a hue scope. A scope set with hueScope also moves the accent family onto its hue (see accent). Outside one, hue-icon is the current text color, hue-tint is faint and hue-soft is tint and hue-fill is the current text color.",
